================================================================================
3D SYNCHRONOUS INTENT GRID - PHASE 1
================================================================================

Directive: 3D_parallel_grid_and_MRH_abstraction.md

Testing whether 3D synchronous parallel CA can produce oscillations
that 1D sequential CA could not (Sessions #18-25: 0/808).

Key differences:
  - 3D geometry: Can form closed cavities with mode structure
  - Synchronous update: Preserves isotropy, all cells compute simultaneously
  - GPU parallel: Scales to millions of cells

